From: Caelestia++ <caelestia-plus-plus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:37:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(requests): stop sending Connection: close

Connection-specific headers are forbidden in HTTP/2 (RFC 7540 8.1.2.2). Qt
up to 6.11.1 dropped this one when it negotiated h2; 6.11.2 forwards it,
ipinfo, nominatim and open-meteo reset the stream, and every Requests.get
ends in "HTTP/2 protocol error". There was no connection to keep alive
here in the first place.
---
 plugin/src/Caelestia/requests.cpp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plugin/src/Caelestia/requests.cpp b/plugin/src/Caelestia/requests.cpp
index 862dea7..b4dd999 100644
--- a/plugin/src/Caelestia/requests.cpp
+++ b/plugin/src/Caelestia/requests.cpp
@@ -26,7 +26,6 @@ void Requests::get(const QUrl& url, QJSValue onSuccess, QJSValue onError, QJSVal
     request.setAttribute(QNetworkRequest::CookieSaveControlAttribute, QNetworkRequest::Manual);
     request.setRawHeader("Cache-Control", "no-cache, no-store");
     request.setRawHeader("Pragma", "no-cache");
-    request.setRawHeader("Connection", "close");
 
     if (headers.isObject()) {
         QJSValueIterator it(headers);
